        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 66-year-old male patient, admitted on 04/12/2019 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Blood tests were obtained to exclude infectious or other systemic causes. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, with good clinical response. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. The patient was discharged on 05/12/2019 in a stable condition. I recommend continuation of his inhaler regimen and close follow-up in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you have any questions.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Hospital course note"
                }
              ]
